  "description": "Monthly median and observed minimum-to-maximum significant wave height at Bilinga, 2025.",
  "usermeta": {
    "title": "How Did Wave Conditions Change at Bilinga in 2025?",
    "analysis": "Wave conditions at Bilinga varied markedly throughout 2025. May had the highest monthly median significant wave height (1.20 m), while July had the lowest (0.58 m). March stood out for its extremes, with a maximum of 4.87 m compared with a monthly median of 1.15 m. Of the year's 521 valid half-hourly observations reaching at least 2 m, 452 occurred in March, coinciding with the major swell associated with Tropical Cyclone Alfred. The difference between March's peak and May's higher median shows that short-lived extreme conditions and a consistently elevated typical wave height are not the same. The next chart examines whether seasonal differences in typical conditions recur across 2022–2025.",
    "method": "Queensland Government Bilinga wave buoy: 30-minute 2025 observations in AEST. Of 17,520 observations, 515 missing-value readings coded -99.9 were excluded. The line represents monthly medians and the shaded area spans the observed minimum to maximum of 17,005 valid significant wave-height observations.",
